SEL relays: ``peat parse -d selrelay`` can now parse individual settings files (``SET_*.TXT``), directories of relay files (``SET_ALL.TXT`` is reconstructed from ``CFG.TXT`` and ``SET_*.TXT`` if it's missing), output of the ``SHOW`` (``SHO``) command, and every relay in a QuickSet ``.rdb`` file. Pulls from relays without a ``SET_ALL.TXT`` now rebuild it from the individual settings files. Added tests with a real SEL-710 QuickSet database, and documented the formats.
